Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: yappari-leste
Source: https://github.com/smatkovi/yappari-leste
Comment:
 Yappari for Maemo Leste is a port of Yappari 2.0.27 for Maemo 5
 (https://github.com/agamez/yappari). Most source files of Yappari carry a
 BSD 2-clause notice, while the Debian packaging of Yappari declared the
 package GPL-2+; both are reproduced below.
 .
 The binary package also contains yappari-wa, built from backend/ with Go.
 It statically links third-party Go modules, among them whatsmeow
 (MPL-2.0) and go.mau.fi/libsignal (GPL-3.0), so the yappari-wa binary as
 a whole is distributed under the GPL-3.0. The exact module versions are
 listed in backend/go.mod and backend/go.sum.

